Use shared schemas in apps/api/docs/prototype/swagger.yaml

Generated on 2026-11-24. Apply AFTER the other two patches, from the
repository root:

  git apply apps/api/docs/prototype/claude-exploration/api-patch-001-recommended-changes.patch
  git apply apps/api/docs/prototype/claude-exploration/api-patch-002-shared-responses.patch
  git apply apps/api/docs/prototype/claude-exploration/api-patch-003-shared-schemas.patch

Adds 3 schemas to #/components/schemas/ and refers to them with $ref:

- DateOfBirthAccuracy: the 27-value list and its 3-paragraph
  description, previously copied in the POST /children/search body,
  dobAccuracyHeaderParameter and DateOfBirth.accuracyIndicator. The
  header parameter's own description is shortened to point to the
  schema.
- StageId: used by stageidParameter, Stage.stageid and
  StageStatusResponse.stageid. Also fixes POST /children/{ypid}/stages/,
  whose response pointed stage_id at a parameter instead of a schema.
- Ypid: used by ypidParameter and the POST /children response.
  MinimalChild.ypid now uses it too, so it changes from
  `type: number, format: integer` to an integer from 1 to 999999999,
  nullable for POST /children. Fixes the typo "identifer".

Not included (by the user's choice): sharing schema_version and
supersedes between the POST .../stages/ body and Stage, and a shared
search-criteria schema. attachment_ids items are attachment IDs, not
stage IDs, so they don't use StageId.

